  "query_preview": "discussion for more details.\n\nLONG TERM.../Sunday through Tuesday/...\nRain continues across the panhandle as we move out of the weekend\nand into the week. However, rain rates appear to be lightening up\nfrom moderate and persistent to light and showery over the day \nSunday. There could be periods of heavier showers on the inner \neastern part of the panhandle -- Juneau, Petersburg, Wrangell -- \nthrough the day Monday. Winds across the panhandle continue to \ndiminish through the day Sunday as the low jumps onto land in the \nwestern gulf. High winds from channeling the previous day have the\npotential to linger in the inner channels across the panhandle \nwith models picking up on Stephens Passage in particular. At the \nsame time, winds in Lynn Canal look to increase through the day \nSunday and be sustained around 20 mph as the pressure gradient \nover the panhandle squeezes.",
